      "widgets_values": [
        "## Writing the video description\n\nThe **Video description** node builds this shape for you from its fields; this note is what each\nfield is for. H3 reads one prose block, not a tag list. What reliably works, in this order:\n\n1. **`look`** - one sentence: \"photoreal, same face/hair/outfit as the starting image\". Repeating\n   the identity is what keeps it from drifting mid-clip (the blurred background is added for you).\n2. **`beats`** - one per line; the node turns them into `[0.0s-1.2s] ...` timestamps. Say what the *body* does\n   (blink, breathe, turn, tuck hair, smile) and what the *camera* does (hold, drift in, gentle\n   handheld). Small human motions read far better than big ones at 5 s.\n3. **`dialogue`** - one line each, no quotes needed. H3 lip-syncs it and speaks it. Keep it to one\n   or two short lines for a 5 s clip (about 2.5 words a second); the node warns when it's more.\n   To place a line at a moment, mention it in that beat (\"they say the line below\").\n4. **`audio`** - voice character, then background. If you do *not* want music, say\n   \"no music\" - silence is not the default.\n5. **`avoid`** - the negative tail: \"no cuts, no scene changes, no text overlays, no extra fingers\".\n\nRules of thumb: one continuous shot per 5 s clip; describe motion, never a still pose; do not\nre-describe the scenery the starting image already shows (the model can see it) - spend the words\non movement, speech, and what must *not* change."
      ],
      "title": "How to write the description"
    },
